# Defect 211, 2026-10-04: no golden form ran the control arm, `check
# --permissive`, Part 11's measurement with the thesis rules dropped, so what
# it says could change with every golden green (panel 187's R3). Here, at the
# parse stage: `if n >` over a deeper line is joined by the lexer, and the
# normal arm refuses the join (`continuation_outside_brackets`, a thesis rule);
# the control arm reads the parse as a language without that rule does
# (`selfhost/parse.hero`'s `control`), so it tells the joined head's missing
# body, where until defects 130 and 131 it told nothing at all.

function main()
    n = 1
    if n >
        print(1)  #~v missing_body
